Your swing goes wide again. The flame-cage's claws drive through the gap in your mail for 8 damage, and your four remaining hit points are gone. You drop onto the cold stair at 0 hit points, and the lantern light swims above you.

The Anvil Father's hand holds you for a while. Your first death save succeeds (15), and the cage's next stab at you misses. Your second fails (4). Then the cage's claw finds you again, a critical hit, and the blow counts as two more failures. That makes three.

Brakka Ironvein is dead.

Up in the gallery Dorrin hears the fight go quiet. He waits with the pick in his shaking hands, and the blue light creeps up the stair behind the silence. Tamsin and old Orrick still lie chained on their slabs, and sunrise will still come to Greyhollow.

The story does not have to end here. If you like, we can make a new character, who will come into the same world, with the town, the mine, the missing miners and the clock still running. Or you can go back to before a line of yours and play on from there, changing a choice. Which would you like?


